# Gate step 1173-a5ng — data, not code.
#
# Binds the fixture for the salvage-ledger trunk fallback. Hermetic: every arm
# builds a throwaway git repo with its own EMPTY-but-reachable origin and a local
# branch standing in for trunk, so nothing touches this checkout's ledger,
# contacts the real origin, or deletes a ref.
#
# THE ARM THAT MATTERS IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL: a line absent from origin and
# unmarked in BOTH copies must still refuse. The fallback asks whether TRUNK
# carries the MARKER, not whether trunk carries the line — widen that by one
# word and every outstanding rescue is forgiven silently, which is the opposite
# of what this ledger exists for.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the salvage ledger consults trunk before calling a deleted ref an outstanding rescue (1173-a5ng)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-salvage-refs-ledger.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the salvage-ledger trunk fallback regressed (1173-a5ng) — either a behind tree is again refused for a line trunk already marked (which refuses every in-flight gate in the fleet the moment a ref is deleted), or the fallback has widened and a genuinely outstanding rescue is being forgiven; see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="salvage-refs ledger trunk fallback check passed"
# Exit 3 means the checker is absent — nothing was examined, and the fixture
# says so by name rather than passing.
STEP_SKIP_EXIT=3
STEP_SKIP_DESC="scripts/check-salvage-refs-ledger.sh is absent, so the fallback could not be exercised"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="macneo 2026-09-22 darwin ok:   sweep-salvage-refs.sh states the one-pass-after-the-marker deletion rule"
